51
00:02:58,780 --> 00:03:03,300
[Episode 3: "Spotlight"]

52
00:03:03,960 --> 00:03:05,280
You did well yesterday.

53
00:03:07,190 --> 00:03:08,190
But...

54
00:03:10,790 --> 00:03:12,420
don't ever do it again.

55
00:03:12,800 --> 00:03:14,190
Do you know
how dangerous that was?

56
00:03:14,610 --> 00:03:16,520
You probably won't be as lucky next time.

57
00:03:17,140 --> 00:03:18,680
There were so many staff around.

58
00:03:18,700 --> 00:03:20,220
Let them handle it.

59
00:03:22,390 --> 00:03:23,340
I'm sorry.

60
00:03:25,860 --> 00:03:27,530
I heard something about the workshop.

61
00:03:28,020 --> 00:03:29,410
You didn't do very well, did you?

62
00:03:31,900 --> 00:03:32,540
Yes.

63
00:03:33,280 --> 00:03:35,260
I want to see you put in more effort.

64
00:03:35,490 --> 00:03:36,190
Well...

65
00:03:36,500 --> 00:03:39,220
I'm not sure if I can do it.

66
00:03:39,420 --> 00:03:40,520
I get it,

67
00:03:41,520 --> 00:03:42,890
but you do realize

68
00:03:42,950 --> 00:03:44,700
this is real business, right?

69
00:03:45,090 --> 00:03:46,900
You need to learn to be more responsible.

70
00:03:46,920 --> 00:03:47,570
Yes...

71
00:03:47,590 --> 00:03:49,300
An opportunity has presented itself,

72
00:03:49,510 --> 00:03:50,940
one that's hard to come by.

73
00:03:51,030 --> 00:03:51,810
You've already seized it,

74
00:03:51,829 --> 00:03:53,140
so don't let it slip through your fingers.

75
00:03:54,610 --> 00:03:55,240
Yes.

76
00:03:57,350 --> 00:03:58,520
That's all I have to say.

77
00:03:59,030 --> 00:03:59,980
Keep your chin up.

78
00:04:10,590 --> 00:04:11,980
Go wait outside for now, Wan.

79
00:04:12,670 --> 00:04:14,110
Cher, stay and talk to me for a bit.

80
00:04:16,110 --> 00:04:17,620
Thank you, Wut.

81
00:04:19,290 --> 00:04:21,100
Put on a confident face.

82
00:04:23,900 --> 00:04:24,900
Do it right.

83
00:04:32,810 --> 00:04:33,810
Ugh...

84
00:04:34,710 --> 00:04:35,980
Was I stern enough?!

85
00:04:36,810 --> 00:04:37,890
You were good.

86
00:04:37,909 --> 00:04:39,740
He was already shivering enough.

87
00:04:42,720 --> 00:04:44,260
Good thing I took
acting classes in high school.

88
00:04:44,590 --> 00:04:45,690
I was president of the club.

89
00:04:47,000 --> 00:04:48,610
I remember that course...

90
00:04:49,820 --> 00:04:50,510
Alright,

91
00:04:51,640 --> 00:04:53,220
this is too soon for us to relax.

92
00:04:54,840 --> 00:04:57,250
An insider just reported that

93
00:04:57,270 --> 00:04:59,740
they're holding a meeting about Wan today.

94
00:05:02,830 --> 00:05:03,900
Well, yesterday,

95
00:05:04,070 --> 00:05:06,290
he upstaged everyone else.

96
00:05:06,510 --> 00:05:08,100
This is gonna be an epic battle.

97
00:05:09,400 --> 00:05:10,660
Then...

98
00:05:11,900 --> 00:05:13,940
go work your magic.

99
00:05:14,290 --> 00:05:15,810
I know you've got this.

100
00:05:16,700 --> 00:05:17,820
As for Wan...

101
00:05:17,990 --> 00:05:20,340
I'll take him somewhere
so I can work my magic.

102
00:05:24,630 --> 00:05:25,620
Best of luck!

103
00:05:30,230 --> 00:05:31,820
Wan, sweetie!

104
00:05:32,909 --> 00:05:34,510
She gets to play the angel all alone

105
00:05:34,800 --> 00:05:36,600
while I'm stuck here being a villain.

106
00:05:40,920 --> 00:05:43,060
Ugh! What a day.

107
00:05:43,380 --> 00:05:44,700
My villain era...

108
00:05:54,270 --> 00:05:54,990
Quick!

109
00:06:21,090 --> 00:06:22,940
Is this really gonna work, Cher?

110
00:06:24,120 --> 00:06:25,140
Absolutely.

111
00:06:26,740 --> 00:06:28,980
He dwells here because of its good energy.

112
00:06:29,300 --> 00:06:30,700
He doesn't just take any clients, though.

113
00:06:30,860 --> 00:06:31,980
You need a secret code.

114
00:06:48,990 --> 00:06:50,020
Come on.

115
00:07:00,570 --> 00:07:01,500
Peek-a-boo!

116
00:07:03,300 --> 00:07:05,340
I'll make you famous in all three realms.

117
00:07:05,730 --> 00:07:06,500
After this,

118
00:07:06,520 --> 00:07:07,810
you'll get booked for sure.

119
00:07:32,310 --> 00:07:35,690
She sells seashells by the seashore.

120
00:07:35,710 --> 00:07:39,290
Happy birthday to you, happy birth...

121
00:07:44,520 --> 00:07:45,520
Peek-a-boo!

122
00:07:47,440 --> 00:07:48,530
You are now reborn.

123
00:07:52,909 --> 00:07:54,500
I heard there are international fans.

124
00:07:55,020 --> 00:07:57,620
I will chant in English for you.

125
00:07:57,909 --> 00:07:59,170
Master, then please...

126
00:07:59,190 --> 00:08:00,090
throw in Korean

127
00:08:00,110 --> 00:08:00,890
and Japanese.

128
00:08:00,910 --> 00:08:02,020
Oh, no sweat.

129
00:08:04,010 --> 00:08:06,540
How much wood
would a woodchuck chuck...

130
00:08:08,310 --> 00:08:11,330
I scream, you scream,
we all scream for ice cream.

131
00:08:11,350 --> 00:08:12,320
A clam cram in a clean cream can.

132
00:08:12,340 --> 00:08:12,900
Hm?

133
00:08:13,790 --> 00:08:15,640
Adam ate an apple,
and Amanda ate an apricot.

134
00:08:15,660 --> 00:08:16,270
Hm?

135
00:08:16,290 --> 00:08:19,140
Silly Sally sings spring songs,
sitting by swiftly swirling streams.

136
00:08:22,620 --> 00:08:23,860
Mm...

137
00:08:25,130 --> 00:08:26,270
You feel the power?

138
00:08:26,300 --> 00:08:27,380
To the max.

139
00:08:29,340 --> 00:08:30,860
With a bit of bleeding gums, by the way.

140
00:08:33,330 --> 00:08:34,700
Then, should we head out?

141
00:08:35,220 --> 00:08:36,929
- I'm heading out.
- Thank you.

142
00:08:36,950 --> 00:08:37,720
Thank you.

143
00:08:37,740 --> 00:08:38,460
Thank you.

144
00:08:38,480 --> 00:08:39,179
Thank you.

145
00:08:39,200 --> 00:08:40,880
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

146
00:08:42,230 --> 00:08:43,710
Good luck. May you flourish.

147
00:08:43,960 --> 00:08:44,850
Sure thing.

148
00:08:45,250 --> 00:08:46,670
Don't do this in Las Vegas, okay?

149
00:08:46,710 --> 00:08:47,700
Hard pass.

150
00:09:05,300 --> 00:09:08,180
My face will get more laughs
than Master's incantations, Cher.

151
00:09:09,220 --> 00:09:09,860
Boo!

152
00:09:13,790 --> 00:09:16,100
Do we really have to go the extra mile?

153
00:09:16,810 --> 00:09:17,680
Come on.

154
00:09:17,980 --> 00:09:20,420
If you don't believe in it,
it's just a gold mask treatment.

155
00:09:21,290 --> 00:09:22,540
Though I can feel

156
00:09:22,710 --> 00:09:24,400
something good happening.

157
00:09:24,760 --> 00:09:26,310
Once anointed, always flourishing!

158
00:09:27,310 --> 00:09:29,380
So, do I go to the workshop like this?

159
00:09:29,980 --> 00:09:31,340
Well, you can rub it off.

160
00:09:31,560 --> 00:09:33,000
I think the spell's already been absorbed.

161
00:09:35,560 --> 00:09:37,420
Well, how many languages have been absorbed?

162
00:09:37,660 --> 00:09:39,510
I'll leave it on for another three minutes.

163
00:09:46,940 --> 00:09:49,100
Wan is not capable of playing Sky.

164
00:09:49,600 --> 00:09:50,900
We'll have to recast.

165
00:09:51,820 --> 00:09:53,500
He doesn't pay attention,

166
00:09:53,700 --> 00:09:54,860
memorize the script,

167
00:09:55,120 --> 00:09:56,780
or read the novel.

168
00:09:58,140 --> 00:09:59,300
Most importantly...

169
00:09:59,800 --> 00:10:01,190
he was late.

170
00:10:02,310 --> 00:10:05,260
He doesn't have it in him
to be a good actor.

171
00:10:06,300 --> 00:10:07,390
Third and Nine said the same.

172
00:10:08,120 --> 00:10:09,300
But what can we do?

173
00:10:09,510 --> 00:10:11,310
As long as that kid is still playing Sky,

174
00:10:11,390 --> 00:10:13,780
I think the quality of our series will suffer.

175
00:10:14,320 --> 00:10:16,220
One rotten apple with bad acting

176
00:10:16,710 --> 00:10:17,980
spoils the whole barrel.

177
00:10:18,210 --> 00:10:20,500
Also, we don't have that much time.

178
00:10:20,660 --> 00:10:21,700
I say...

179
00:10:21,720 --> 00:10:23,910
wouldn't it be easier if we got someone

180
00:10:24,410 --> 00:10:25,780
who already has the skills?

181
00:10:25,800 --> 00:10:26,740
I agree,

182
00:10:26,880 --> 00:10:28,280
because the role of Sky

183
00:10:28,300 --> 00:10:30,120
- can still be recast.
- Mm.

184
00:10:30,140 --> 00:10:32,020
And I have this boy

185
00:10:32,190 --> 00:10:33,140
named Time

186
00:10:33,400 --> 00:10:35,500
who also auditioned and did an amazing job.

187
00:10:35,820 --> 00:10:37,040
Time...

188
00:10:38,230 --> 00:10:39,860
He auditioned for Heart, right?

189
00:10:39,880 --> 00:10:40,700
Yeah?

190
00:10:40,720 --> 00:10:41,500
That's correct.

191
00:10:41,940 --> 00:10:42,800
Interesting.

192
00:10:43,680 --> 00:10:44,430
But I think...

193
00:10:44,450 --> 00:10:46,210
Time's image

194
00:10:46,660 --> 00:10:48,170
doesn't really match Sky's.

195
00:10:48,190 --> 00:10:50,780
We can just adjust his character to fit Sky.

196
00:10:51,310 --> 00:10:52,660
Wouldn't that be easier?

197
00:10:53,000 --> 00:10:53,700
Alright,

198
00:10:53,940 --> 00:10:54,790
I'll make the final call myself.

199
00:10:55,540 --> 00:10:56,540
We'll go with Time.

200
00:10:56,810 --> 00:10:57,340
Fabulous!

201
00:10:57,750 --> 00:10:58,390
Sure thing.

202
00:11:01,400 --> 00:11:02,500
This little meeting,

203
00:11:02,870 --> 00:11:04,500
is it about removing Wan?

204
00:11:05,960 --> 00:11:07,060
Right now,

205
00:11:07,100 --> 00:11:08,980
wouldn't you say Wan
is the one creating the most buzz

206
00:11:09,640 --> 00:11:10,860
in 'The Deep Between Us'?

207
00:11:13,100 --> 00:11:14,380
What are you on about?

208
00:11:14,400 --> 00:11:15,260
Are you fucking lost?!

209
00:11:15,300 --> 00:11:16,200
I'm not.

210
00:11:16,430 --> 00:11:17,340
You're the one who's lost.

211
00:11:17,870 --> 00:11:19,940
You do nothing but scheme
to remove someone else's boy.

212
00:11:19,960 --> 00:11:21,430
Have you even checked
the social media buzz?

213
00:11:21,450 --> 00:11:22,760
Well, buzz...

214
00:11:22,780 --> 00:11:24,100
comes and goes.

215
00:11:24,410 --> 00:11:25,880
Still, we have to thank Wan

216
00:11:26,790 --> 00:11:29,200
for giving
'The Deep Between Us' more exposure.

217
00:11:29,440 --> 00:11:31,000
But I've already
made the decision, you see.

218
00:11:31,900 --> 00:11:32,810
Alright...

219
00:11:33,640 --> 00:11:34,910
then Renji is also out.

220
00:11:36,400 --> 00:11:38,020
And I'm not entirely sure

221
00:11:38,040 --> 00:11:39,380
if lately...

222
00:11:39,800 --> 00:11:41,860
you've talked to Da Xiang?

223
00:11:42,110 --> 00:11:43,900
The messages they sent,

224
00:11:44,190 --> 00:11:45,710
have you checked them?

225
00:11:46,290 --> 00:11:47,050
Why do I have to?

226
00:11:47,070 --> 00:11:48,110
Oh, I don't know.

227
00:11:48,510 --> 00:11:50,220
But I recommend you do.

228
00:11:55,030 --> 00:11:56,970
Wan's viral right now...

229
00:11:56,990 --> 00:11:57,900
Good job.

230
00:12:09,220 --> 00:12:10,080
You won.

231
00:12:11,510 --> 00:12:13,700
Though you have to groom Wan properly

232
00:12:14,380 --> 00:12:16,580
because his problems right now
are his acting

233
00:12:16,600 --> 00:12:17,900
and discipline.

234
00:12:18,370 --> 00:12:19,940
And if he doesn't do better,

235
00:12:20,120 --> 00:12:21,990
I will put out a statement
about how unready he is,

236
00:12:22,230 --> 00:12:24,620
along with the list
of all the real reasons.

237
00:12:26,900 --> 00:12:28,660
As a director,

238
00:12:29,100 --> 00:12:31,020
I'd say that Wan has a knack for it.

239
00:12:31,790 --> 00:12:33,700
And in the previous workshop,

240
00:12:34,110 --> 00:12:36,220
it's not like Wan couldn't act at all.

241
00:12:36,630 --> 00:12:37,890
Besides,

242
00:12:37,910 --> 00:12:39,170
we have our acting coach,

243
00:12:39,190 --> 00:12:40,140
Luang,

244
00:12:40,700 --> 00:12:42,540
and judging from that outfit,

245
00:12:42,650 --> 00:12:43,680
I'd say...

246
00:12:43,820 --> 00:12:46,220
he has the skills of a master.

247
00:12:46,950 --> 00:12:47,850
Could you manage?

248
00:12:50,570 --> 00:12:51,880
Then...

249
00:12:52,840 --> 00:12:53,900
that settles it.

250
00:12:55,200 --> 00:12:56,380
If you'll excuse me.

251
00:12:56,720 --> 00:12:58,680
Wasting my time with this kind of talk,

252
00:12:58,700 --> 00:13:01,580
ugh, I should've been talking to
tens of clients who...

253
00:13:01,600 --> 00:13:04,340
want to work with Wan.

254
00:13:15,430 --> 00:13:16,980
North, you've promised, though,

255
00:13:17,000 --> 00:13:18,090
that even if Time doesn't get Sky,

256
00:13:18,110 --> 00:13:19,380
you'll find him another role,

257
00:13:19,410 --> 00:13:20,410
or else I won't have it!

258
00:13:20,440 --> 00:13:21,650
Alright, I've already told you

259
00:13:21,670 --> 00:13:23,490
that he's definitely
gonna get something!

260
00:13:25,410 --> 00:13:26,500
Pai, I'll leave it to you.

261
00:13:28,820 --> 00:13:30,180
And it all circles back to me...

262
00:13:36,410 --> 00:13:38,280
Have you seen all the hype around Wan?

263
00:13:38,800 --> 00:13:39,950
So many fans are saying that

264
00:13:39,970 --> 00:13:42,100
he's the perfect fit for Sky,

265
00:13:42,120 --> 00:13:44,350
and that his character is spot on!

266
00:13:44,370 --> 00:13:45,880
Come on, let me see.

267
00:13:46,320 --> 00:13:47,500
Oh, look at him go!

268
00:13:48,100 --> 00:13:48,810
[Fits the character perfectly]

269
00:13:48,830 --> 00:13:49,460
[Is Wan Sky, or is Sky Wan?
I'm confused; he strutted out of the novel]

270
00:13:49,480 --> 00:13:50,740
Gotta admit,

271
00:13:50,830 --> 00:13:52,020
Wan is

272
00:13:52,210 --> 00:13:54,500
the picture-perfect casting choice
for Sky from the novel.

273
00:13:55,290 --> 00:13:56,580
Oh, my God...

274
00:13:56,990 --> 00:13:58,820
That means we'll have to work hard.

275
00:13:59,260 --> 00:14:00,110
It's our job.

276
00:14:00,130 --> 00:14:01,380
We have to work hard regardless.

277
00:14:01,610 --> 00:14:02,680
But this is, like, so hard.

278
00:14:02,700 --> 00:14:04,500
Well, maybe dress down.

279
00:14:05,200 --> 00:14:06,110
Wan,

280
00:14:06,140 --> 00:14:08,220
